const n={toc:[{id:"nail-art-styles-at-a-glance",text:"Nail Art Styles at a Glance",level:2},{id:"nail-art-ideas-by-occasion",text:"Nail Art Ideas by Occasion",level:2},{id:"weddings-and-bridal",text:"Weddings and bridal",level:3},{id:"party-nights",text:"Party nights",level:3},{id:"office-friendly",text:"Office-friendly",level:3},{id:"festive-occasions",text:"Festive occasions",level:3},{id:"everyday-chic",text:"Everyday chic",level:3},{id:"occasion-guide-at-a-glance",text:"Occasion Guide at a Glance",level:2},{id:"choosing-colours-for-your-nail-art",text:"Choosing Colours for Your Nail Art",level:2},{id:"picking-a-nail-shape",text:"Picking a Nail Shape",level:2},{id:"gel-polish-vs-regular-polish",text:"Gel Polish vs Regular Polish",level:2},{id:"natural-nails-extensions-or-overlays",text:"Natural Nails, Extensions or Overlays?",level:2},{id:"how-to-bring-your-inspiration",text:"How to Bring Your Inspiration",level:2},{id:"before-your-nail-art-appointment",text:"Before Your Nail Art Appointment",level:2},{id:"making-your-nail-art-last",text:"Making Your Nail Art Last",level:2},{id:"pair-it-with-a-manicure",text:"Pair It With a Manicure",level:2},{id:"book-your-nail-art-in-bangalore",text:"Book Your Nail Art in Bangalore",level:2}],before:`<p>Nail art is one of the easiest ways to finish a look, whether you&#39;re dressing up for a wedding or just want something fresh for the week. But with so many styles available, it&#39;s hard to know where to start. These <strong>nail art ideas</strong> are organised by occasion, so you can choose a design that suits the event, your outfit and your routine.</p>
<p>We&#39;ll also explain the difference between gel and regular polish, how to bring your inspiration to your appointment, and how to make your nail art last.</p>
<h2 id="nail-art-styles-at-a-glance">Nail Art Styles at a Glance</h2>
<p>Before choosing by occasion, here&#39;s a quick look at the styles available at Xing Premium Unisex Salon:</p>
<p><strong>Finishes</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Gel Polish:</strong> rich, glossy colour cured under a lamp for a long-wearing finish</li>
<li><strong>Chrome:</strong> a high-shine, mirror-like metallic finish</li>
<li><strong>Cat Eye:</strong> a magnetic shimmer that moves with the light</li>
<li><strong>Galaxy:</strong> deep, starry, multi-tone designs with sparkle</li>
<li><strong>Glitter:</strong> from subtle shimmer to full sparkle</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Classics</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>French Tips:</strong> clean, elegant tips, classic white or any colour</li>
<li><strong>Ombre:</strong> a seamless colour fade</li>
<li><strong>Liner Art:</strong> fine lines and minimal patterns</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Designer Art</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Marble Art:</strong> elegant marble swirls</li>
<li><strong>3D Art:</strong> raised, sculpted designs</li>
<li><strong>Dry Flower:</strong> real dried flowers set into your design</li>
<li><strong>Stone:</strong> rhinestones and embellishments</li>
<li><strong>Sticker Art:</strong> fun, detailed designs applied with nail stickers</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="nail-art-ideas-by-occasion">Nail Art Ideas by Occasion</h2>
<h3 id="weddings-and-bridal">Weddings and bridal</h3>
<p>Wedding nails need to look elegant, photograph well and complement heavy outfits and jewellery.</p>
<p><strong>Try:</strong> French tips, chrome, or stone-embellished designs.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>French tips</strong> are timeless and pair with any outfit</li>
<li><strong>Chrome</strong> adds a subtle, glamorous shine</li>
<li><strong>Stone</strong> adds sparkle that echoes bridal jewellery</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Tip:</strong> bring a photo of your outfit and jewellery so your nail artist can match tones.</p>
<h3 id="party-nights">Party nights</h3>
<p>Parties are the time to have fun with sparkle and shine.</p>
<p><strong>Try:</strong> glitter, galaxy or cat eye.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Glitter</strong> catches the light on the dance floor</li>
<li><strong>Galaxy</strong> gives a deep, starry, dramatic look</li>
<li><strong>Cat eye</strong> shifts and glows as you move</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="office-friendly">Office-friendly</h3>
<p>Workplace nails should look neat, polished and understated.</p>
<p><strong>Try:</strong> gel polish, ombre or liner art.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Gel polish</strong> in a nude, soft pink or deep classic shade looks polished for days</li>
<li><strong>Ombre</strong> in soft tones is subtle but stylish</li>
<li><strong>Liner art</strong> adds a modern touch without being loud</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="festive-occasions">Festive occasions</h3>
<p>Festivals call for colour, sparkle and a celebratory feel.</p>
<p><strong>Try:</strong> stone, glitter or 3D art.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Stone</strong> adds a traditional, embellished feel</li>
<li><strong>Glitter</strong> in gold or rich colours suits festive outfits</li>
<li><strong>3D art</strong> makes a statement for special celebrations</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="everyday-chic">Everyday chic</h3>
<p>For everyday wear, choose designs that are pretty but easy to live with.</p>
<p><strong>Try:</strong> French tips, marble or dry flower.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>French tips</strong> in a soft colour look fresh every day</li>
<li><strong>Marble</strong> looks sophisticated and luxe</li>
<li><strong>Dry flower</strong> adds a delicate, botanical touch</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="occasion-guide-at-a-glance">Occasion Guide at a Glance</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Occasion</th>
<th>Nail art ideas</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td>Wedding and bridal</td>
<td>French tips, stone, chrome</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Party night</td>
<td>Glitter, galaxy, cat eye</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Office-friendly</td>
<td>Gel polish, ombre, liner art</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Festive</td>
<td>Stone, glitter, 3D art</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Everyday chic</td>
<td>French tips, marble, dry flower</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
`,after:`<h2 id="choosing-colours-for-your-nail-art">Choosing Colours for Your Nail Art</h2>
<p>The colour matters as much as the design. A few simple guidelines:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Match your outfit, not exactly but in tone.</strong> Pick a shade from the embroidery or jewellery rather than the main colour of the outfit.</li>
<li><strong>Warm skin undertones</strong> often look lovely with gold accents, warm reds, corals and nudes with a peachy base.</li>
<li><strong>Cool undertones</strong> often suit silver accents, berry shades, cool pinks and nudes with a rosy base.</li>
<li><strong>For the office,</strong> nudes, soft pinks, deep reds and classic neutrals always look polished.</li>
<li><strong>For festivals,</strong> rich jewel tones and metallics feel celebratory.</li>
</ul>
<p>If you&#39;re unsure, your nail artist can suggest a palette that suits your skin and outfit.</p>
<h2 id="picking-a-nail-shape">Picking a Nail Shape</h2>
<p>Your nail shape changes how a design looks. Common shapes include:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Square and squoval:</strong> clean and practical, great for French tips and everyday wear</li>
<li><strong>Round and oval:</strong> soft and natural, flattering on shorter nails</li>
<li><strong>Almond:</strong> elegant and lengthening, lovely for bridal designs</li>
<li><strong>Coffin and stiletto:</strong> dramatic shapes that suit bold party designs, usually on extensions</li>
</ul>
<p>Not sure? Your nail technician will suggest a shape that suits your hands and lifestyle.</p>
<h2 id="gel-polish-vs-regular-polish">Gel Polish vs Regular Polish</h2>
<p>Your choice of polish affects how long your nail art looks fresh.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th></th>
<th>Gel Polish</th>
<th>Regular Polish</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td><strong>How it sets</strong></td>
<td>Cured under a lamp</td>
<td>Air-dries</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Finish</strong></td>
<td>Glossy and long-wearing</td>
<td>Quick and easy</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Changing it</strong></td>
<td>Needs professional removal</td>
<td>Easy to change; wears off sooner</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
<p><strong>Choose gel polish</strong> if you want your nails to stay glossy through a wedding week or a busy schedule. Always have it removed professionally; don&#39;t peel it off.</p>
<p><strong>Choose regular polish</strong> if you like changing your colour often.</p>
<h2 id="natural-nails-extensions-or-overlays">Natural Nails, Extensions or Overlays?</h2>
<p>Nail art works on natural nails, extensions and overlays.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Natural nails:</strong> minimal designs like French tips, liner art or a single accent nail look lovely on shorter nails.</li>
<li><strong>Extensions:</strong> add length for bigger, more detailed designs. Read acrylic vs gel vs poly gel to compare systems.</li>
<li><strong>Overlays:</strong> strengthen natural nails without adding length, giving a sturdier base for nail art.</li>
</ul>
<p>Explore our <a href="/services/nail-extensions">nail extensions and overlays</a> if you want more length first.</p>
<h2 id="how-to-bring-your-inspiration">How to Bring Your Inspiration</h2>
<p>The best way to get the design you want is to show it.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Bring two or three photos</strong> from Instagram or Pinterest</li>
<li><strong>Show your outfit colours</strong> for events</li>
<li><strong>Mention your nail shape and length,</strong> or ask your artist to suggest one</li>
<li><strong>Be open to small adaptations.</strong> Your artist may adjust a design to suit your nail shape and length</li>
</ul>
<p>You can share your inspiration on WhatsApp before your appointment too.</p>
<h2 id="before-your-nail-art-appointment">Before Your Nail Art Appointment</h2>
<p>A few small steps help your design go on smoothly and last longer:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Come with clean, bare nails</strong> if you can, or let us know if you have polish or gel to remove.</li>
<li><strong>Skip hand cream on the day,</strong> as oils can stop polish gripping well.</li>
<li><strong>Decide on length first.</strong> If you want longer nails, book extensions before or alongside your nail art.</li>
<li><strong>Allow enough time.</strong> Detailed designs like 3D art, stones or dry flowers take longer than a single colour or French tips, so mention your design when you book.</li>
<li><strong>Think about your week ahead.</strong> If you&#39;ll be cooking, cleaning or travelling a lot, a sturdier design on gel polish may suit you better.</li>
<li><strong>Share your inspiration in advance</strong> on WhatsApp, so your artist can plan the design before you arrive.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="making-your-nail-art-last">Making Your Nail Art Last</h2>
<ul>
<li>Apply cuticle oil daily</li>
<li>Wear gloves for cleaning and washing dishes</li>
<li>Avoid using your nails as tools</li>
<li>Don&#39;t peel off gel polish; book a professional removal</li>
<li>For events, book one to two days before</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="pair-it-with-a-manicure">Pair It With a Manicure</h2>
<p>A <a href="/services/manicure">manicure and pedicure</a> before your nail art keeps cuticles neat and hands soft, so your design looks even better. Many clients book them together before weddings and festivals.</p>
<h2 id="book-your-nail-art-in-bangalore">Book Your Nail Art in Bangalore</h2>
<p>The right design depends on the occasion: elegant French tips, chrome and stone for weddings; glitter, galaxy and cat eye for parties; gel polish, ombre and liner art for the office; and pretty, easy designs for every day.</p>
<p>Browse our full range of <a href="/services/nail-art">nail art styles</a>, then send us your inspiration photos on WhatsApp and book at Xing Premium Unisex Salon in Sarjapur Road, HSR Layout or Brookfield.</p>
`,takeaways:["Match your nail art to the occasion: bridal, party, office, festive or everyday.","Gel polish gives a glossy, long-wearing finish but needs professional removal; regular polish is easier to change.","Bring two or three inspiration photos, and your outfit colours, to your appointment.","Nail art works on natural nails, extensions and overlays.","For events, book your nail art one to two days before."],faqs:[{q:"Which nail art is best for a wedding?",a:"Popular bridal choices include French tips, chrome and stone-embellished designs. Book your nail art one to two days before the event."},{q:"Can you recreate a nail design from Instagram or Pinterest?",a:"Yes. Share your inspiration photo on WhatsApp or at your appointment, and our nail artist will recreate it or adapt it to your nail shape and length."},{q:"What's the difference between gel polish and regular polish?",a:"Gel polish is cured under a lamp for a glossy, long-wearing finish and needs professional removal. Regular polish air-dries and is easier to change often."},{q:"Can I get nail art on short natural nails?",a:"Yes. Nail art works on natural nails, extensions and overlays. Minimal designs like liner art, French tips or a single accent nail look great on shorter nails."}]};export{n as default};
